    "id": "wp_75",
    "title": "HOOKUP CULTURE AND RELATIONSHIPS: IS CASUAL SEX LIBERATING AND HARMLESS?",
    "slug": "hookup-culture-and-relationships-is-casual-sex-liberating-and-harmless",
    "coverImageUrl": "https://thepublisherspen.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/image.png?w=1024",
    "excerpt": "It is beautiful to discover that individuals who answer questions around this topic view sex in hookup and relationships on different levels. The innate desire for sex in itself is not a wrong desire. It is a desire woven into our being, ju",
    "body": "<p class=\"has-text-align-justify wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"0ec6\">It is beautiful to discover that individuals who answer questions around this topic view sex in hookup and relationships on different levels. The innate desire for sex in itself is not a wrong desire. It is a desire woven into our being, just like the desire for tangibles like food, clothes, and money, and intangibles like fulfillment, love, and so on. While it is baffling to some that a Holy God could create something as pleasurable as sex, others simply embrace it in their own way, free of such questions.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-justify wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"bc79\">However, the term &#8220;casual sex&#8221; raises suspicions among many. The concept of combining &#8220;casual&#8221; with something as intimate as sex feels strange since the two do not belong together. When it comes to casual sex, people have quite different opinions. While some argue that sex needs commitment, others believe it is devoid of responsibility. In summary, you’ll see that they have created a third strand for what you thought was a yes-or-no answer, saying that when there is commitment, sex is not casual; but when there is no commitment, sex is casual. Our cultural norms seem to lean into this split, normalizing sex without strings in many circles.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-justify wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"098a\">Hookup culture, which is a collection of ideas and behaviors that promote having sex without expecting a relationship, is an example of this change. It has been influenced by decades of shifting attitudes and has gained popularity since the sexual revolution of the 1960s. It is frequently associated with urban life and university campuses. The term &#8220;hookup&#8221; is different from prostitution, which emphasizes consensual, non-committal interactions, even though some people associate it with Gen Z slang.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-justify wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"e189\">Hookup culture celebrates freedom, but I think we are easily trivializing sex: someone gets promoted and celebrates with a fling; someone who is stressed out or reeling from a breakup uses sex to relax. It has become a currency that is used to express gratitude for a favor or to feel something, anything. This shift suggests a deeper truth: we know sex is meant for more than just a few moments, but our actions often contradict this. This raises the question: Was sex intended for such relationships, or is there a specific context for it? According to Christian doctrine, sex was intended for the holy setting of marriage. According to this perspective, extramarital sex (whether casual or in a relationship) misses its original purpose and is classified as adultery or fornication.</p>\n\n\n\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"has-text-align-justify wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"75a0\"><em>&#8220;Marriage is to be held in honour among all, and the marriage bed is to be undefiled; for God will judge the sexually immoral and adulterers,&#8221; </em>according to Hebrews 13:4 (NASB). This implies a heavenly norm where deviation has both spiritual and practical repercussions. Unwanted pregnancies, STIs, and psychological damage like loneliness or trust issues are all real-world consequences of casual sex.</p>\n</blockquote>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"999c\">According to Ephesians 5:5 (NASB),</p>\n\n\n\n<blockquote class=\"wp-block-quote is-layout-flow wp-block-quote-is-layout-flow\">\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"45a6\"><em>&#8220;For this you know with certainty, that no sexually immoral or impure or greedy person, which amounts to an idolater, has an inheritance in the kingdom of Christ and God&#8221;.</em></p>\n</blockquote>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"b87f\">Sexual sin is peculiar because, in addition to the eternal stakes, 1 Corinthians 6:18 warns that it damages the body, which is supposed to honour God.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-justify wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"cadd\">Some people&nbsp;believe that uncommitted, casual sex is liberating because it allows for experimentation or liberty. They find nothing wrong with shared pleasure and place a higher priority on consent and satisfaction. From a biblical perspective, however, this freedom might turn into a trap. In many cases, what begins as an adrenaline rush turns into addictive routines that leave people exhausted yet unable to quit. According to psychology, having casual sex might make some people feel less confident or regret it, especially if their emotional needs are not satisfied.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-justify wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"4dc3\">This has nothing to do with condemnation. No matter how far we’ve gone, there is always a way out thanks to God’s love. &#8220;There is therefore no condemnation to them which are in Christ Jesus, who walk not after the flesh but after the Spirit,&#8221; says Romans 8:1 (KJV). When we feel unworthy, that is precisely why we should turn to God, who offers us forgiveness, restoration, and a new beginning. His grace releases us from cycles of reliance or guilt in addition to covering our transgressions. Instant satisfaction is promised by hookup culture, yet pursuing pleasure on its own frequently results in emptiness. God created joy; thus, He is not against it. The context makes a difference: marital pleasure fosters connection rather than bondage. Seeking God, whether via scripture, prayer, or community, gives us a sense of purpose rather than ephemeral joys. The Holy Spirit leads you towards freedom and completeness as you follow a map, uncertain of every step, much like in a treasure hunt.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"3382\">Written by Etokimo Idongesit</p>",
    "author": "Etokimo Idongesit",
    "categories": [
      "Relationships",
      "Purity"
    ],
